# Files excluded from the HCP Terraform upload (S6 infra).
#
# UPLOAD ROOT: the dev and prod workspaces set the working directory to
# envs/<env>. The Terraform CLI is run from infra/envs/<env> and uploads the
# configuration tree one level up from the working directory, that is the infra/
# directory, so the modules next to envs/ travel with it. This file therefore sits
# at infra/, which is the upload root. The same patterns are repeated in
# infra/envs/dev and infra/envs/prod in case a CLI reads the ignore file at the
# working directory instead; a static test keeps the three files identical.
#
# Patterns follow the Terraform CLI ignore rules, which are anchored at the upload
# root, so every pattern is written with a **/ twin to match at any depth. When
# this file exists it replaces the CLI defaults, so the defaults are repeated here.
# Private values never travel with the upload: real backend and variable files stay
# on the owner machine, and workspace variables in HCP carry the values instead.
#
# infra/build/ (the Lambda zips written by scripts/release.sh) is deliberately
# NOT listed here: a remote plan and apply read the zips from the uploaded
# configuration, so they must travel with it. The folder is git-ignored instead.

# Real private configuration (only the .example files are committed)
cloud.auto.tfbackend
**/cloud.auto.tfbackend
terraform.tfvars
**/terraform.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
**/*.tfvars.json
*.auto.tfvars
**/*.auto.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars.json
**/*.auto.tfvars.json

# Key material and local environment files
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.p12
**/*.p12

# Local state and plan artefacts
.terraform/
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
**/*.tfplan
tfplan
**/tfplan
crash.log
**/crash.log
crash.*.log
**/crash.*.log

# Version control metadata
.git/
**/.git/
.gitignore
